WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.902
-Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's team

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.770
is speaking out
about their final report.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.906
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.910
♪♪

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.312
The one thing --
maybe the only thing --

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.982
Donald Trump loves
about being president

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.817
is campaigning for president.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.220
Whenever he's in the White House
doing his actual job,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.656
he looks like he's waiting
in a doctor's office

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.124
for a colonoscopy.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:29.328
But then, when he's on stage,
in front of his adoring fans,

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.430
he lights up.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.364
I mean,
just look at the difference.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:37.269
It's like the before-and-after
from a Prozac commercial.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:39.939
That is the face of a man who
just heard the phrase,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.242
"Good news, there are
no criminal charges."

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.677
In fact,
Trump was clearly ecstatic

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.813
after his attorney general,
William Barr, sent a letter

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.848
claiming that Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's report

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.516
had not established a conspiracy

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.051
between Trump's campaign
and Russia.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.687
And Trump has spent
nearly two weeks celebrating,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.090
despite the fact
that he doesn't actually know

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.424
what's in Mueller's report.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.592
-It's a disgrace what happened.

00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:05.831
This was a terrible thing
that was put onto our country.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.600
Nobody's seen
anything like this.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.569
Probably never happened before.

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:13.873
Beautiful conclusion.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.809
I haven't seen the report.
Beautiful conclusion.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.178
-A beautiful conclu--

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.813
You just said
you hadn't seen the report.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.016
I'd love to hear his summary
of "The Sixth Sense."

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.951
"I haven't seen the movie,
but it's beau--

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:28.221
everyone's alive at the end."

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.056
And even...

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:33.993
Even if you had seen the report,
it's nearly 400 pages.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.528
There's no way you'd be able

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.697
to actually make it
to the conclusion.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.999
I doubt you've ever read
anything that long in your life.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.934
If you locked Trump in a room
and told him,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.170
"Don't come out until
you've read the whole report,"

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.538
you'd open the door the next day

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.406
and see him surrounded
by Big Mac wrappers

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:48.508
and cans of Red Bull,

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.442
hair disheveled,
bags under his eyes,

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:51.877
and you'd say,
"How far have you gotten?"

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:55.915
and he'd go, "So far, Matt.
'Written by Robert Mueller.'

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.349
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.919
And then I hit the wall."

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.887
Still, even though Trump
has not seen the report,

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:03.756
he cannot help
but ramble on and on

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.526
about how he'd been vindicated
and how he defeated his critics

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.160
at a rally in Michigan
last week.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:13.399
-After three years of lies
and smears and slander,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.469
the Russia hoax is finally dead.

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:20.773
The collusion delusion is over.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.376
They tried to divide
our country,

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.412
to poison the national debate,

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:31.417
and to tear up the fabric
of our great democracy.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:37.256
And they're on...artificial
respirators right now.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.425
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:43.062
They're getting
mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.098
-They need
mouth-to-mouth resuscitation?

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.367
Every time you do a rally,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.502
you look like a guy
in an episode of "Baywatch"

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.204
who fell off a party boat and
got dragged back to the beach

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.507
by David Hasselhoff.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.476
When you give a speech,

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:01.180
you suck in air like
you're about to go underwater.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.518
-[ Inhaling ]

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.053
-So, Trump's handpicked attorney
general looked over the report,

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.556
decided Trump had been
exonerated, Trump celebrated,

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:13.693
and we all took his word for it
and moved on, until last night,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.494
when Mueller's team
started to speak out.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.862
-Breaking news overnight.

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:19.331
The New York Times reveals
the Mueller report

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.734
may be far more damaging
for President Trump

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.269
than Attorney General Bill Barr
has led on.

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:27.273
The Times says some of
Robert Mueller's investigators

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.109
have told close associates
that Bill Barr did not

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.877
adequately capture the findings

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:33.913
of the nearly
two-year-long probe

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.049
in his four-page summary
to Congress.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.382
-And the fact
that we're even hearing this

00:03:37.382 --> 00:03:38.551
really means something

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.386
because the Mueller team
never leaks to the press.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.821
I mean, look at him.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.591
Robert Mueller's wife still
doesn't know his middle name.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:48.027
"That's between me
and the government."

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.096
So, now they're saying
Barr's summary,

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.731
the one Trump spent two weeks
celebrating, is inaccurate.

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.867
Wow, when Trump heard that,
he needed...

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.903
-Mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.539
-Look, we don't know
what's in the full report.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.042
We have no idea
if there's anything shocking

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.311
or significantly different
from what's in the Barr summary,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.946
but it's remarkable
that Mueller's team

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.480
is suddenly speaking out
to reporters

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.984
after two years of
total and complete silence.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.386
It's like when you try to get
the Queen's Guard to flinch,

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.254
and they're just
totally still for an hour,

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.357
and then you go, "Let's
get in line for the tour,"

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.192
and they say,
"It's called a queue."

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.228
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.865
Mueller's team
is apparently frustrated

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:29.201
in part because they actually
wrote up several summaries

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.370
of their findings themselves
for public consumption,

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.272
and Barr ignored
all those summaries

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.573
and chose to write his own

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.809
that said the president
had been exonerated.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.411
-Mueller's team
had written some summaries

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:40.713
around this report,
and that those summaries,

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.648
they anticipated,
would be something

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.717
that Barr could use
to be made public,

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:45.785
and that it wasn't,

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.653
and so there's
frustration there.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:49.322
-"The Special Counsel's
investigators

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:52.725
had already written multiple
summaries of the report,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.627
and some team members believe

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:58.630
that Mr. Barr should have
included more of their material

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.967
in the four-page letter
he wrote on March 24th

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.437
laying out
their main conclusions."

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:07.173
-So Mueller's team wrote their
own summaries for the public,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.875
and Barr chose to ignore those
summaries and write his own.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.777
As a general rule,
I'm always suspicious

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:13.579
of anyone who chooses
to do more work

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.214
when they have
the option not to.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.350
I mean, we don't actually write
a new "Closer Look" every night.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.388
We just buy it from a website
called politicalrants.com.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.757
Tonight's "Closer Look"
was written by...

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:25.792
Gary from Oregon.

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.959
Thank you, Gary.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.729
[ Applause ]
Give it up for Gary, everyone.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.602
The "It's called a queue" line
went better than I thought.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:39.605
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:43.008
Republicans have been eager
to declare Trump exonerated

00:05:43.008 --> 00:05:44.410
and quickly move on
from all that

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.944
rather than wait
for the full report.

00:05:45.944 --> 00:05:47.312
In fact,
Trump and his aides have said

00:05:47.312 --> 00:05:48.715
they want to take their victory

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:51.050
and set the stage
for the 2020 election.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.284
Last week, for example,

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:54.320
Trump's former strategist
Steve Bannon

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.322
took human form
and appeared on CNN

00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:59.925
to tell Anderson Cooper
he didn't think any Democrat

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.594
could compete with Trump
in 2020.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:02.928
-At the end of the day,

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.164
the Democrats, I think,
are gonna focus on somebody

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.399
who can beat Donald Trump,

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.133
and they're gonna search
for that.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.036
It's not gonna be
a policy discussion.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.837
It's gonna be electability.

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:14.273
And if you're gonna beat
Donald Trump as an incumbent,

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:15.507
you're gonna have to bring it,
right?

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:16.709
You're gonna really
have to bring it.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.444
In the field I've seen so far,

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.180
I don't know anybody
that can hit a fast ball

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.814
like Donald Trump can throw.

00:06:22.814 --> 00:06:23.949
-First of all, Steve,

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:26.152
thank you for joining us
from the other side.

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.853
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:29.088
What's going on with you, man?

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:33.359
You look like the ghost
of a dead ghost.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.493
I mean...

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.795
[ Applause ]

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:39.565
That whole thing
looked like an interview

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.167
with a before-and-after
of a guy who takes Prozac

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.736
and a guy who snorts it.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.237
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.240
Second, of all the things that
you can say about Donald Trump,

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.440
he cannot throw a fast ball.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.309
Have you ever seen him
throw out the first pitch

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.377
at a baseball game?

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.845
Look at his face.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:53.946
He looks like he's farting

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.782
and pulling a muscle
at the same time.

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:59.018
This is why we need to see
the full Mueller report

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.186
as soon as possible.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:02.020
For two years, we've been
waiting for answers,

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.857
and instead, we've been getting
lies from the president

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.792
and unconfirmed rumors
going from...

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:08.460
-Mouth-to-mouth.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.963
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

